<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-nim-refused-p02769> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-nim-refused-p02769> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The hosted BioNeMo ESMFold endpoint refused a fold request for bovine serum albumin with HTTP 401 and the message \"Invalid JWT serialization: Missing dot delimiter(s)\" when called with the key supplied on 31 October 2026." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-nim-refused-p02769> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "A smoke test of the hosted BioNeMo ESMFold NIM on Albumin from Bos taurus (UniProt P02769, residues 25-607, 583 aa) did not run: the service rejected the credential. The attempt, its timestamp, the HTTP status and the server's own message are recorded rather than discarded, so the next person does not assume the route works. Meta's public ESM Atlas endpoint was used instead for the thread's structure predictions." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-nim-refused-p02769> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "method observation (service refusal)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-nim-refused-p02769> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "One request, 2026-10-31T13:18:56.765Z, endpoint https://health.api.nvidia.com/v1/biology/nvidia/esmfold. Key taken from the process environment, never stored. No fallback, retry or second key was tried. The claim is about this request and this credential, nothing wider." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-nim-refused-p02769> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/organism-esmfold-P02769-refusal-record> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-nim-refused-p02769> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Repeat the identical request with a key whose prefix is \"nvapi-\". A 200 response carrying a structure would show the route is sound and the refusal was the credential; a second 401 would point at the account or the endpoint instead." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-nim-refused-p02769> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Does not establish: that the endpoint is unavailable, misconfigured or unusable, or that ESMFold would fail on this sequence. It records one authentication failure with one credential at one time." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/organism-esmfold-nim-refused-p02769> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch09-06> .
}
<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/provenance> {
  <http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasAttributedTo> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#SoftwareAgent> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "organism-design/esmfold/smoke-test.mjs: calls a hosted ESMFold service on one checksummed UniProt sequence and records what happened." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "organism-design/esmfold/smoke-test.mjs" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> <https://schema.org/codeRepository> <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-organism-esmfold-client> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/esmfold-v1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/esmfold-v1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/esmfold-v1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ESMFold v1, a protein language model with a structure head" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/esmfold-v1> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "esmfold-v1" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/esmfold-v1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The version string is the one the service itself reports in the PDB TITLE record of each prediction." .
}
